  "description": "This course covers image processing fundamentals including pixel manipulation, filtering, and edge detection using OpenCV and NumPy; feature extraction techniques such as SIFT, SURF, and ORB for image matching and object recognition; object detection with YOLOv8 and SSD models; image segmentation using U-Net and Mask R-CNN architectures; 3D vision with stereo vision and depth estimation; camera calibration using OpenCV's calibrateCamera function; and computer vision applications in robotics and autonomous systems. Students will explore image enhancement methods like histogram equalization and contrast adjustment; analyze image data using OpenCV's image processing pipelines; and implement real-time vision systems using Python and OpenCV libraries.",
